      "text": "From $\\mathbf{M}^T \\mathbf{M} = \\mathbf{I},$ we have\n\\[\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & x & x \\\\ 2y & y & -y \\\\ z & -z & z \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 2y & z \\\\ x & y & -z \\\\ x & -y & z \\end{pmatrix} = \\mathbf{I}.\\]Then\n\\begin{align*}\n0 &= (0)(0) + (x)(x) + (x)(x) \\\\\n&= x^2 + x^2 \\\\\n&= 2x^2.\n\\end{align*}Therefore, $x = 0$ or $x = \\pm 1.$  Now,\n\\begin{align*}\n2y^2 &= 0^2 + (x)(x) + ((-1)(-1)) \\\\\n&= x^2 + 1 \\\\\n&= 1 + 1 \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{align*}and\n\\begin{align*}\nz^2 &= 0^2 + (x)(2y) + (x)(x) \\\\\n&= x(2y) + x^2 \\\\\n&= 2y(1) + 1 \\\\\n&= \\boxed{2}.\n\\end{align*}. The answer is 2",
